<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Sultanate of Shewa</h1><p class="st-meta">896 CE – 1285 CE (approx.) · capital Walale</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the earliest Muslim states of the Ethiopian interior, ruled by the Makhzumi dynasty in eastern Shewa.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>According to a late Arabic chronicle, the Makhzumi dynasty, claiming descent from an Arab clan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, founded a sultanate in eastern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-shewa">Shewa</a> in 896. The date and the dynasty's origins are uncertain, but the state reflects the spread of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> inland from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-aden">Gulf of Aden</a> along <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a> linking the coast at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeila">Zeila</a> with the highlands.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Very little is known about its government. It was a Muslim trading state among largely non-Muslim neighbours, dealing in slaves, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and highland produce passed down to the coast. In the 13th century it was weakened by succession disputes among rival members of the dynasty, which gave outside powers a chance to intervene.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1285 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umar-walasma">Umar Walasma</a>, ruler of neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifat-sultanate">Ifat</a>, conquered the sultanate and absorbed it into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-ifat">Sultanate of Ifat</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walashma-dynasty">Walasma</a> dynasty that followed carried on Muslim power in the region for two more centuries.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sultanate-of-shewa.jpg" alt="Sultanate of Shewa" width="320" height="358"><figcaption>Image: Aldan-2 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sultanate_of_Showa.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>896 CE – 1285 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Walale</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Shewa Sultanate, Sultanate of Showa, Makhzumi Sultanate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1090&amp;focus=sultanate-of-shewa" aria-label="Sultanate of Shewa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5745 1884 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sultanate of Shewa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6094 2113h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6065 2140h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M6065 2140h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Ethiopia. <a href="/atlas?year=1090&amp;focus=sultanate-of-shewa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
